ENTRY            C3134   20260717   20261014   20261014       C259
SUBENT        C3134001   20260717   20261014   20261014       C259
BIB                 12         41
TITLE      Single-Nucleon Transfer on Unstable 59Cu Probes the
           NiCu Cycle in Astrophysical X-Ray Bursts
AUTHOR     (C.O'Shea,G.Lotay,A.Gade,D.T.Doherty,H.Schatz,
           J.S.Randhawa,B.A.Brown,D.Weisshaar,J.Pereira,
           S.A.Gillespie,D.W.Bardayan,S.Byrne,L.Canete,
           W.N.Catford,G.Cerizza,A.Chester,J.Chung-Jung,
           C.Cousins,S.Coil,H.L.Crawford,S.Giraud,E.Good,
           G.Grauvogel,I.Harca,J.Heery,A.Hill,R.Jain,C.Maher,
           F.Montes,C.Muller-Gatermann,S.Noji,N.D.Pathirana,
           T.Parry,C.Paxman,A.M.Rogers,A.Sebastian,I.Sultana,
           J.A.Swartz,A.Tsantiri,S.Uthayakumaar,R.G.T.Zegers)
REFERENCE  (J,PRL,137,022701,2026)
           #doi:10.1103/gbbj-hpqk
INSTITUTE  (2UK SUR,1USAMSU,1USALAS,1USANOT,1USALTI,1USABRK,
           1USAANL,1USACMG)
FACILITY   (LINAC,1USAMSU) The FRIB linear accelerator.
INC-SPECT  A beam of radioactive 59Cu ions at 40 MeV/nucleon was
           produced by projectile fragmentation of a
           240-MeV/nucleon primary beam of 64Zn ions from the
           FRIB linear accelerator. This beam, with an average
           purity of >99% and intensity ~8*10**6 pps.
DETECTOR   (HPGE,MAGSP) The GRETINA array with S800 magnetic
           spectrograph.
SAMPLE     A 7.5-mg/cm2-thick deuterated polyethylene target(CD2).
METHOD     (TOF,EDE,GSPEC) A combination of time-of-flight and
           dE measurements were used to identify residues on an
           event-by-event basis. Doppler-shift corrections for
           gamma-ray energies were based on the 60Zn velocity
           vectors ray-traced through the S800 and the precise
           spatial coordinates of gamma-ray interactions within
           GRETINA. Characteristic gamma rays were measured in
           Doppler-corrected singles and gamma-gamma-gated
           spectra to establish the level scheme. Finally,
           background contributions from the 59Cu(12C,11B)
           reaction were determined from a separate measurement
           using a 9.6-mg/cm2-thick polyethylene (CH2) target.
ANALYSIS   (INTAD) Angle-integrated cross sections for 60Zn were
           extracted from observed gamma-ray intensities.
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) All quoted uncertainties are given at the
           1 sigma (68%) confidence level.
HISTORY    (20260717C) BP
